{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99017","id":2171419483,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6BbTtb","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99017","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99017.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99017.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99017","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99017/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99017/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99017/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/8137cdaccf515c9ac571b69d628958a059d67fe2","number":99017,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix top-Level CollisionShapes with Area2D","user":{"login":"tGautot","id":44877251,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODc3MjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44877251?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tGautot","html_url":"https://github.com/tGautot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tGautot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tGautot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tGautot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tGautot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tGautot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tGautot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tGautot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tGautot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tGautot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Very first godot PR, and even time looking at godotengine's code, please roast anything as needed as my understanding is quite limited.\r\n\r\nIn the physics server, shapes are simple data structure without reference to the canvas, mostly just the shape itself (circle/rect/...) and its transform. This transform was always expected to be relative to the parent object's transform, meaning that a CollisionShape2D marked as top level would never behave as such.\r\n\r\nBy adding a new field to these shapes (indpdt_xform) representing whether it is top_level, the final tranform computations done in GodotArea2Pair2D (that get then passed to the collision solver) can be adjusted to be relative or not.\r\n\r\nFor the update of the `top_level` field, since it causes a change in the final transform, i decided to piggy back on top of the `set_shape_transform` functions, meaning that any needed update would be triggered. Also, I didn't create a new specialized `set_shape_top_level` function as that could have lead to needing some change in the `CollisionShape2D::_update_in_shape_owner` to avoid triggering multiple changes to `GodotPhysicsServer2D::godot_singleton->pending_shape_update_list` lower down the line. I feel like `transform` and `top_level` are very linked, but feel free to contest that choice.\r\nBecause the signature of some functions have been changed, I made sure to set default values in the different bindings to avoid gdscript compatibility breakage, even though some of those default values are definitely counter-intuitive to use (i.e. the `set_shape_transform` has a default value of false for `top_level` meaning if it is created as top level and then the transform is updated without care, the top level might be lost).\r\nI also added a warning to CollisionShape2D nodes with `top_level` (saying that it is experimental) based on  @rburing 's recommendations.\r\n\r\n\r\nAs a first step, this PR only add this top_level feature to collision shapes working with areas, not bodies. \r\n\r\nI have quite a limited view and understanding of the whole physics engine, I tested my changes in multiple ways and couldn't find something breaking. Please notify me of any doubts you might have regarding normal behaviour.\r\n\r\n* *Bugsquad edit, fixes: #98741*","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708059,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4MDU5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_ur